What is Amazon Machine Image (AMI)?
Last Updated : 17 Dec, 2025

An Amazon Machine Image (AMI) is a template that contains the software configuration (operating system, application server, and applications) required to launch an Amazon EC2 instance.

Think of an AMI as the "blueprint" for your virtual server. You cannot launch an EC2 instance without specifying an AMI. Whether you launch one instance or thousands, they all start as a clone of the AMI you select.
